{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MadronichSpectra",
    "description": "Stage 3 of WRF-Chem's Madronich photolysis (phot_opt = 1): the temperature- and pressure-dependent absorption cross sections and quantum yields that SUBROUTINE subgrid builds on top of the static xs/xqy tables (chem/module_phot_mad.F:2326-2445 and :2519-2530, WRF v4.8.0).\n\nIt is a POINT component in (T, n_air) producing 101-bin spectra, not a column component, because that is what the physics is: the Fortran's s(lev,kl,nr), qy(lev,kl,nr) and ao3(lay,kl) are the same functions of the local temperature and air density evaluated on different grids. Mounting it at an interface temperature gives s and qy; mounting it at a layer-mean temperature gives ao3. Both are tested here, which is the cheapest possible demonstration that they are one function.\n\nEleven spectra are rebuilt from the local state: the ozone cross section (linear in T between the NASA-JPL-2011 218 K and 295 K spectra, FLAT outside that range), the O(1D) and O(3P) quantum yields (the FTUV fo3qy form of Matsumi et al. 2002, which McKeen substituted in 2013 for the older arctan fit -- the old code is still in the file, commented out), the pressure-quenched formaldehyde molecular channel, the four Stern-Volmer quenched dicarbonyl yields, and acetone, which methyl ethyl ketone simply copies.\n\nA NOTE ON THE TWO IDIOSYNCRASIES this project flagged earlier, now checked against the dumped tables rather than the comments. The WRF comment `ch3coo2h 20 actually use 0.28*(h2o2 value)` describes how the xs(:,20) COLUMN WAS BUILT, not a relation the code evaluates: the measured ratio xs(:,20)/xs(:,10) over the 60 bins where both are non-zero is NOT constant, it ranges from 0.1414 to 0.2874 and clusters near 0.276. Likewise `hcocho=chcho 18 estimate, no reliable measurement` is a note on the provenance of a stored 64-bin spectrum. Both are therefore reproduced by transcribing the tables, not by a formula -- but the point stands that an implementation built from the literature rather than from these tables will not match, because no literature spectrum for peroxyacetic acid is 0.276 times hydrogen peroxide's. Those two static tables are NOT in this component; they arrive with the wavelength-integration stage that consumes them.\n\nBins: the scheme uses kl0..kl1 = 30..130 of its 130-bin grid, so this component carries the 101 active bins. Outside that range the Fortran never initialises qy at all."
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NBIN": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 101,
      "description": "Number of active wavelength bins, kl1-kl0+1 = 101."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "wlbin": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NBIN"
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MadronichSpectra": {
      "subsystems": {
        "par": {
          "ref": "./madronich_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "T": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "K",
          "default": 250.0,
          "description": "Temperature at which the spectra are evaluated. Mount this component at the INTERFACE temperature zt(lev) to get photolysis_mad's s(lev,:,:) and qy(lev,:,:); mount it at the LAYER-MEAN temperature vt(lay) to get ao3(lay,:). The Fortran spells the two out separately (module_phot_mad.F:2432-2440 and :2521-2529) but they are the same function of T."
        },
        "n_air": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "cm^-3",
          "default": 2.5e+19,
          "description": "Air number density at the same point, zair(lev). Only the pressure-quenched yields read it."
        },
        "t_frac": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Interpolation weight between the 218 K and 295 K ozone spectra, clamped to [0, 1]."
        },
        "sigma_o3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^2",
          "description": "Ozone absorption cross section. This is s(lev,kl,2) when T is an interface temperature and ao3(lay,kl) when T is a layer mean.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "sigma_o3_o3p": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^2",
          "description": "Cross section of the O3 -> O(3P) channel; identical to the O(1D) one, s(lev,kl,3) = s(lev,kl,2).",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "kt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^-1",
          "description": "0.695 T, the thermal energy in wavenumbers used by the O(1D) yield."
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Boltzmann population of the upper O3 vibrational state, exp(-825.518/kT)."
        },
        "q_frac1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "q1/(q1+q2) with q1 = 1."
        },
        "q_frac2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "q2/(q1+q2)."
        },
        "tau": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "T/300, the reduced temperature of the O(1D) yield."
        },
        "qy_o1d_mid": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The 305-328 nm branch of the O(1D) yield, evaluated everywhere and selected by the branch below.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_o1d": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Quantum yield of O3 + hv -> O(1D), the FTUV fo3qy form (Matsumi et al. 2002) that McKeen put in for NASA-JPL-2011. 0.90 below 305 nm, the four-term fit to 328 nm, a flat 0.08 to 340 nm, and zero above.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_o3p": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Quantum yield of O3 + hv -> O(3P), 1 - qy_o1d by construction.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "phi1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Tabulated radical-channel yield of CH2O, xqy(:,11).",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "phi2": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Tabulated molecular-channel yield of CH2O, xqy(:,12), floored so the untaken branch of the ifelse below stays finite.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "phi20": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "1 - phi1, the zero-pressure molecular yield.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "ak300": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^3",
          "description": "Quenching rate parameter at 300 K.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "akt": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "cm^3",
          "description": "Quenching rate parameter at T, with the 61.69 temperature/wavelength term.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_ch2o_mol_raw": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Molecular CH2O yield before clipping.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_ch2o_mol": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Quantum yield of CH2O + hv -> H2 + CO, pressure-quenched above 330 nm and clipped to [0, 1]. This is RADM2's j_ch2om.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "sv_ratio": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "n_air/2.465e19, the Stern-Volmer density ratio."
        },
        "qy_ch3cho": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Quantum yield of CH3CHO photolysis, Stern-Volmer quenched. RADM2's j_ch3cho.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_glyoxal_a": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Glyoxal channel a yield, Stern-Volmer quenched. RADM2's j_hcocho.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_mgly": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Methylglyoxal yield, Stern-Volmer quenched. RADM2's j_ch3cocho.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_glyoxal_b": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Glyoxal channel b yield, Stern-Volmer quenched. RADM2's j_hcochob.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_acetone": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Acetone yield, 0.0766 + 0.09415 exp(-n_air/3.222e18). RADM2's j_ch3coch3 -- which RADM2 also uses for OP2, its higher organic peroxide.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        },
        "qy_mek": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Methyl ethyl ketone yield; the Fortran sets qy(:,15) = qy(:,14) outright. RADM2's j_ch3coc2h5.",
          "shape": [
            "wlbin"
          ]
        }
      },
